# THE BUILD OUTPUT IS NOT THE SOURCE, and here that distinction is 2 GB.
#
# `dist/` holds win-unpacked, linux-unpacked, the AppImage staging tree and the installers - every one
# of them a full copy of the editor plus an Electron runtime. Committing it would push the binaries
# into git history, where they stay forever even after a later delete, and it would put the previous
# build's copies (`dist/_prev-*`) there too.
#
# The source-available promise is satisfied by the SOURCE being here and by the release carrying
# the licence.
# Binaries belong on the Releases page, attached to a tag, where the signed manifest already points.
dist/
node_modules/

# electron-builder's own scratch: a per-run debug dump that names absolute paths on the build machine.
builder-debug.yml
dist_electron/

# The signed release documents are produced per build from a key that is not in this repository.
# They are published by attaching them to a release, never by committing them.
*.pem
payload.json
stable.json
beta.json

*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
